# 075 · Model usage for each run, campaign and the whole system

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Running campaigns

## What

Every model call the agents make is counted, and control shows the totals:

- **Per call** (code records it, never an agent): the agent kind (workers, planner, teachers, auditor, review panel), the harness, the provider and the model; tokens in, split into cached and not cached where the provider says; tokens out (and reasoning tokens where the provider says); the time to the first token and the whole call's time, so output tokens a second.
- **A run's Overview:** the totals and the speed (tokens out a second, median and spread), for each agent kind and model.
- **A campaign's page:** the same, summed over all its runs, with each run's share.
- **The whole system** (Overview): the same over every campaign and rig, for a period (today, 7 days, all).
- **REST and MCP:** the same numbers, so they can be read without the dashboard.
- Where a harness does not report a figure (for example cached tokens), the screen says "not reported", never 0.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-21: "overview on a capmaign run doesn't show total tokens used etc... Would love some model stats (tok/s, total tokens in / out / cache / not-cached, etc...)... And a roll up to campaign for all runs under it, and a roll up to entire system."

## Done when

- [ ] The harness and the supervisor record each model call's usage and time, for every harness (Pi, OpenCode, Codex, Claude Code), as far as each reports it; the rig sends it to control with its events.
- [ ] Control sums it per run, per campaign and for the system; REST and MCP give the sums.
- [ ] The run's Overview, the campaign's page and the system Overview show them, after a mockup the owner approved.
- [ ] Tests for the records, the sums and the "not reported" case; pages updated.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-21, owner, on the mockup (`v010-usage`): "top of run page, side bar of campaign page, stats page for top level across the system (metrics tab)." So: a run's model use at the top of its page; a campaign's in its page's sidebar; the system's on a new **Metrics** page in the main navigation. The mockup's other choices are built as shown: no cost column, the median time to the first token, and "today" in the viewer's own time zone.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-21: Goal written from the owner's words. Trials already record tokens in and out (`trial_finished`); cached tokens, the planner's and advisors' calls, and times are not recorded yet. A mockup comes first for the screens.

